Each language must have correct navigation, page metadata, descriptions, calls to action, accessible labels, and relevant alternate-page links.

Use the approved canonical narrative as the source for content. Do not invent live metrics, features, user counts, divine approvals, certifications, or deployment statuses.

The design should be sophisticated and futuristic without sacrificing clarity, accessibility, responsive behavior, reduced-motion support, or performance.

Do not create a competing frontend if the current `apps/dock` application is the correct public website.

